WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.090
Welcome to the Singularity Daily, Sunday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.010
Here's your day in superintelligence, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.240
This week, voters,

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:21.560
investors and Elvis's music owners told the AI industry: we still get a say.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.790
Anthropic's investors now expect $1 to $1.5 trillion. Not two.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.750
Meta's assistant, Muse,

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:39.300
now scores 47% on its Personal Superintelligence Index. Up from 38.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.880
It also remembers what matters: in 90% of tasks, up from 76.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:51.570
And a US lab says it cut a Chinese model's propaganda from 22% to under 1%.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.340
In Tel Aviv, researchers got two AI models to teach each other.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:58.870
No human data at all.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.310
Now, the money. OpenAI banked $11 billion,

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:06.390
at $1.25 trillion. Less than it hoped.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.190
Goldman Sachs reckons the data centre boo

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:12.880
m could cost $8.5 trillion in five years.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.560
Meanwhile, the US cleared Nvidia's AI chips for a Chinese firm with an empty office.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:21.610
Wires dangling.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.380
One man, twelve brands, no employees: AI's his team.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:29.290
He expects up to $3 million this year.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.910
An AI-designed bird flu vaccine from Cambridge fully protected animals.

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.920
Stockpiled ones? About half.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.540
And NYT Cooking's new AI helper saved a reviewer's chicken.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.720
Then it almost ruined her cake.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.300
The catch? Elvis's and Eminem's music owners are suing an AI song maker.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:56.110
Accused of AI, Dior's animator says: "Everything was drawn by hand."

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.420
Now, the machines. In Philadelphia,

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:09.230
a 78-year-old professor blocks delivery robots. She got a ticket.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.270
China's state news agency has two humanoid robot anchors.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:16.140
Their look? By film director Zhang Yimou.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:21.380
Dubai just got a showroom for humanoid robots. Need one? 28 to choose from.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.870
It's all moving fast.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.970
But the future isn't just happening to us. We still get a say.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.670
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.540
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.230
That's the Singularity Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
